<title>SWEDEN: Lithuanian carrier to lease Saab aircraft.</title>
<headline>Lithuanian carrier to lease Saab aircraft.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuanian Airlines will lease two used Saab 340B from Saab Aircraft, a spokesman for Saab said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Lithuania will first lease one and then later a second used Saab 340B aircraft,&quot; Saab Aircraft spokesman Anders Annerfalk told Reuters.</p>
<p>No financial details of the deal could be released according to Saab Aircraft's agreement with Lithuanian Airlines, he said.</p>
<p>Saab Aircraft said earlier on Monday the Lithuanian national carrier had chosen the 33-seat Saab 340B for its regional routes, initially operating on routes to Warsaw, Kiev and Berlin from Vilnius.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1250</p>
